' F10 -- Layered idempotency in the content-addressed ingestion pipeline,
' at the thesis revision (dfc20df6).
' HERO FIGURE. Chapter 4.
' Claim supported: a re-submitted file meets nine mechanisms in four layers;
' eight are live. L0 (the parse-cache replay) is still read on the classic
' route but nothing written at this revision can pass its parser check, so it
' is drawn dashed and grey. Thick borders (stereotype <<content>>) mark the
' mechanisms keyed on the bytes alone and shared by every owner; thin ones are
' keyed per owner, run or lecture. "Per owner" holds for the run row, not for
' the whole stack. Layout: a centred spine (REQ, L1, L3, L4, L5, L7, OK) keeps
' Smetana from staircasing; "note left" is misplaced by Smetana, so one note.
' Sources: cache.py:191-231, upload.py:195-206, file_parse_service.py:1148
' (L0); upload_service.py:105-120 (L1); materials_service.py:90-120,
' upload.py:633-700 (L2); repos.py:44-100, migration 20260730000000:50 (L3);
' unified_orchestrator.py:862-867 (L4); job_locks.py:33-54,
' unified_orchestrator.py:68, :871-877 (L5); :994-998 (L6); :717-748,
' poster.py:116-128, repos.py:483-512 (L7); file_parse_service.py:827-841,
' cache.py:554-556 (L8). Edge case: reconcile.py:45-49, :123-129,
' arq_worker.py:67.
' Size budget: <= 715 x 865 px at 80 dpi, so labels print at >= 6.5 pt.
@startuml f10-idempotency
!include _style.iuml

title Layered idempotency: eight live mechanisms in four layers

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}
skinparam packageStyle frame
<style>
.content {
  LineThickness 2.5
}
.legacy {
  LineThickness 2.5
  LineStyle 5
  FontColor #666666
}
</style>
hide stereotype

rectangle "Re-submission of identical PDF bytes" as REQ #DCDCDC

package "Layer 1 -- Request, before any job" {
  rectangle "**L0  Parse-cache replay**\npdf_parse_cache by pdf_hash,\nclassic route only; nothing\nwritten today passes: no hit" as L0 <<legacy>>
  rectangle "**L1  Content addressing**\nsha256(bytes) is the name:\npdf-uploads/<sha256>.pdf,\nupsert, one object per input" as L1 <<content>>
  rectangle "**L2  Owner dedupe**\nv4: owner's Lesson returned,\nno quota, no job; batch:\nknown bytes skipped" as L2
}

package "Layer 2 -- Database" {
  rectangle "**L3  One run per owner**\nparse_runs UNIQUE (pdf_hash, pipeline_version,\nuser_id); a COALESCE upsert never clobbers" as L3
  rectangle "**L4  Completed-run replay**\ncompleted ==> replay from DB:\nno re-parse, no second lecture" as L4
}

package "Layer 3 -- Redis" {
  rectangle "**L5  In-flight lock**\nSET joblock:parse:<sha256> NX EX 1200\nTTL 1200 s > job_timeout 900 s" as L5 <<content>>
}

package "Layer 4 -- Outputs of a re-parse" {
  rectangle "**L6  Lecture reuse**\nre-parse clears content,\nkeeps lecture_id: links to\nthe lecture survive" as L6
  rectangle "**L7  Upserted outputs**\nreader copy, poster (upsert),\nparse receipt ON CONFLICT\n(run_id)" as L7
  rectangle "**L8  Embedding dedupe**\nsha256(embedding text)\nchecked before any paid\nAPI call" as L8 <<content>>
}

rectangle "At most one parse per owner and pipeline version (unless forced)" as OK #BFBFBF

L0 -[hidden]right- L1
L1 -[hidden]right- L2
L6 -[hidden]right- L7
L7 -[hidden]right- L8

REQ -down-> L1
L1 -down-> L3
L3 -down-> L4
L4 -down-> L5
L5 -down-> L7
L7 -down-> OK

note right of L5
  Best effort: on a Redis error the job
  runs unlocked, so duplicates both parse.
  Hash-keyed: a second owner mid-parse
  stays 'queued' until the 6 h sweep.
end note

legend bottom
  Thick border: keyed on the bytes alone, so shared by every owner. Thin: per owner, run or lecture.
  Dashed and grey: L0 (also keyed on the bytes) is still read on the classic route but cannot hit.
endlegend

@enduml
